IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `aia-core`

-- aia-annex-x: Annex X, "Union legislative acts on large-scale IT systems in the area of Freedom, Security and Justice".
-- Annex X is a list of twelve Union acts. Article 111(1) uses it: an AI system that is a component of a
-- large-scale IT system established by a legal act listed in Annex X, and placed on the market or put into service
-- before 2 August 2027, is to be brought into compliance by 31 December 2030 (aia-timeline.l4, `Art 111(1) ...`).
-- Annex X was not changed by the Omnibus (no passage of it carries a marker in the consolidated text), so there is one version.
-- READ-ONLY for the parts. They call `Annex X the large-scale IT system is established by a listed legal act`.

§ `The table`

-- One row for each act of Annex X, in the Annex's order. `point` and `letter` are the Annex's own numbering
-- (the letter is "" where the point has one act only). `act` is the act's designation, as the Annex writes it up to its
-- first "of the"; the quote lines above the table carry the whole title.
DECLARE `Annex X entry` HAS
    point   IS A NUMBER
    letter  IS A STRING
    system  IS A STRING
    act     IS A STRING

-- src:1887 | ANNEX X
-- src:1888 | Union legislative acts on large-scale IT systems in the area of Freedom, Security and Justice
-- src:1889 | 1. Schengen Information System
-- src:1890 | (a) Regulation (EU) 2018/1860 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 28 November 2018 on the use of the Schengen Information System for the return of illegally staying third-country nationals (OJ L 312, 7.12.2018, p. 1).
-- src:1891 | (b) Regulation (EU) 2018/1861 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 28 November 2018 on the establishment, operation and use of the Schengen Information System (SIS) in the field of border checks, and amending the Convention implementing the Schengen Agreement, and amending and repealing Regulation (EC) No 1987/2006 (OJ L 312, 7.12.2018, p. 14).
-- src:1892 | (c) Regulation (EU) 2018/1862 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 28 November 2018 on the establishment, operation and use of the Schengen Information System (SIS) in the field of police cooperation and judicial cooperation in criminal matters, amending and repealing Council Decision 2007/533/JHA, and repealing Regulation (EC) No 1986/2006 of the European Parliament and of the Council and Commission Decision 2010/261/EU (OJ L 312, 7.12.2018, p. 56).
-- src:1893 | 2. Visa Information System
-- src:1894 | (a) Regulation (EU) 2021/1133 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 7 July 2021 amending Regulations (EU) No 603/2013, (EU) 2016/794, (EU) 2018/1862, (EU) 2019/816 and (EU) 2019/818 as regards the establishment of the conditions for accessing other EU information systems for the purposes of the Visa Information System (OJ L 248, 13.7.2021, p. 1).
-- src:1895 | (b) Regulation (EU) 2021/1134 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 7 July 2021 amending Regulations (EC) No 767/2008, (EC) No 810/2009, (EU) 2016/399, (EU) 2017/2226, (EU) 2018/1240, (EU) 2018/1860, (EU) 2018/1861, (EU) 2019/817 and (EU) 2019/1896 of the European Parliament and of the Council and repealing Council Decisions 2004/512/EC and 2008/633/JHA, for the purpose of reforming the Visa Information System (OJ L 248, 13.7.2021, p. 11).
-- src:1896 | 3. Eurodac
-- src:1897 | Regulation (EU) 2024/1358 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 14 May 2024 on the establishment of ‘Eurodac’ for the comparison of biometric data in order to effectively apply Regulations (EU) 2024/1315 and (EU) 2024/1350 of the European Parliament and of the Council and Council Directive 2001/55/EC and to identify illegally staying third-country nationals and stateless persons and on requests for the comparison with Eurodac data by Member States’ law enforcement authorities and Europol for law enforcement purposes, amending Regulations (EU) 2018/1240 and (EU) 2019/818 of the European Parliament and of the Council and repealing Regulation (EU) No 603/2013 of the European Parliament and of the Council (OJ L, 2024/1358, 22.5.2024, ELI: http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1358/oj).
-- src:1898 | 4. Entry/Exit System
-- src:1899 | Regulation (EU) 2017/2226 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 30 November 2017 establishing an Entry/Exit System (EES) to register entry and exit data and refusal of entry data of third-country nationals crossing the external borders of the Member States and determining the conditions for access to the EES for law enforcement purposes, and amending the Convention implementing the Schengen Agreement and Regulations (EC) No 767/2008 and (EU) No 1077/2011 (OJ L 327, 9.12.2017, p. 20).
-- src:1900 | 5. European Travel Information and Authorisation System
-- src:1901 | (a) Regulation (EU) 2018/1240 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 12 September 2018 establishing a European Travel Information and Authorisation System (ETIAS) and amending Regulations (EU) No 1077/2011, (EU) No 515/2014, (EU) 2016/399, (EU) 2016/1624 and (EU) 2017/2226 (OJ L 236, 19.9.2018, p. 1).
-- src:1902 | (b) Regulation (EU) 2018/1241 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 12 September 2018 amending Regulation (EU) 2016/794 for the purpose of establishing a European Travel Information and Authorisation System (ETIAS) (OJ L 236, 19.9.2018, p. 72).
-- src:1903 | 6. European Criminal Records Information System on third-country nationals and stateless persons
-- src:1904 | Regulation (EU) 2019/816 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 17 April 2019 establishing a centralised system for the identification of Member States holding conviction information on third-country nationals and stateless persons (ECRIS-TCN) to supplement the European Criminal Records Information System and amending Regulation (EU) 2018/1726 (OJ L 135, 22.5.2019, p. 1).
-- src:1905 | 7. Interoperability
-- src:1906 | (a) Regulation (EU) 2019/817 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 20 May 2019 on establishing a framework for interoperability between EU information systems in the field of borders and visa and amending Regulations (EC) No 767/2008, (EU) 2016/399, (EU) 2017/2226, (EU) 2018/1240, (EU) 2018/1726 and (EU) 2018/1861 of the European Parliament and of the Council and Council Decisions 2004/512/EC and 2008/633/JHA (OJ L 135, 22.5.2019, p. 27).
-- src:1907 | (b) Regulation (EU) 2019/818 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 20 May 2019 on establishing a framework for interoperability between EU information systems in the field of police and judicial cooperation, asylum and migration and amending Regulations (EU) 2018/1726, (EU) 2018/1862 and (EU) 2019/816 (OJ L 135, 22.5.2019, p. 85).
@ref Annex X (src:1887-1907)
`Annex X the entries` MEANS
    LIST
        `Annex X entry` 1 "a" "Schengen Information System" "Regulation (EU) 2018/1860"
      , `Annex X entry` 1 "b" "Schengen Information System" "Regulation (EU) 2018/1861"
      , `Annex X entry` 1 "c" "Schengen Information System" "Regulation (EU) 2018/1862"
      , `Annex X entry` 2 "a" "Visa Information System" "Regulation (EU) 2021/1133"
      , `Annex X entry` 2 "b" "Visa Information System" "Regulation (EU) 2021/1134"
      , `Annex X entry` 3 "" "Eurodac" "Regulation (EU) 2024/1358"
      , `Annex X entry` 4 "" "Entry/Exit System" "Regulation (EU) 2017/2226"
      , `Annex X entry` 5 "a" "European Travel Information and Authorisation System" "Regulation (EU) 2018/1240"
      , `Annex X entry` 5 "b" "European Travel Information and Authorisation System" "Regulation (EU) 2018/1241"
      , `Annex X entry` 6 "" "European Criminal Records Information System on third-country nationals and stateless persons" "Regulation (EU) 2019/816"
      , `Annex X entry` 7 "a" "Interoperability" "Regulation (EU) 2019/817"
      , `Annex X entry` 7 "b" "Interoperability" "Regulation (EU) 2019/818"

§ `Questions the table answers`

-- Is the act one of the acts Annex X lists? Article 111(1) speaks of "the legal acts listed in Annex X": the list answers
-- the question which acts those are, so an act that is not on it is not one of them (the ruling of 2026-11-05 on definitions
-- handed to a list; fork F-annex-x-closed in NOTES.md records the other reading, NOTHING).
@ref Annex X (the list), used by Art 111(1)
GIVEN `the act` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Annex X the act is listed` MEANS
    IF any (GIVEN e YIELD e's act EQUALS `the act`) `Annex X the entries`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text hands the question to the list): "the legal acts listed in Annex X" (Art 111(1))

-- The system that an act of the Annex establishes, as the Annex names it. NOTHING where the act is not on the list.
@ref Annex X (the list), used by Art 111(1)
GIVEN `the act` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`Annex X the large-scale IT system the act establishes` MEANS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN e YIELD e's act EQUALS `the act`) `Annex X the entries`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): an act that is not on the list names no Annex X system
    WHEN x FOLLOWED BY rest THEN JUST (x's system)

-- The fact a seat can state: the large-scale IT system the AI system is a component of is established by this act.
-- The result is the input `the AI system is a component of a large-scale IT system established by a legal act listed in Annex X`
-- of aia-timeline.l4's `Art 111(1)` functions.
@ref Annex X (the list), used by Art 111(1)
GIVEN `the AI system is a component of a large-scale IT system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act that establishes that large-scale IT system` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Annex X the large-scale IT system is established by a listed legal act` MEANS
        `the AI system is a component of a large-scale IT system`
    AND `Annex X the act is listed` `the act that establishes that large-scale IT system`
